unar roving vehicle","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","publications":[{"submissionId":19660028019,"id":"7a9c0f59b62d4d6da5c24e4d7dcc26ae","publicationDate":"1966-06-15T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"19660028019.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/19660028019/downloads/19660028019.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/19660028019/downloads/19660028019.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/19660028019/downloads/19660028019.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-10-01-04-12"},{"_meta":{"score":190.69989},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20170000950,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"27130d7f35854afd989c7adf33958b78","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Engineering (General)","Lunar And Planetary Science And Exploration","Numerical Analysis"],"keywords":[" Moon"," wheel"," exploration","Mobility"," tire"," traction"," Mars"," roving vehicle"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20170000950,"ear":"NO","id":"bb951e029d14410b8f5d690b2a1a5a07","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-07-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","otherReportNumbers":["GRC-E-DAA-TN32423","Report Number: GRC-E-DAA-TN32423"],"fundingNumbers":[{"number":"NNC14VH93P","submissionId":20170000950,"id":"6b1311bf2398449c888ce679134f5dfb","type":"CONTRACT_GRANT"},{"number":"WBS 647280.04.03.20","submissionId":20170000950,"id":"199e134f81264c278a7ceb97ba995023","type":"WBS"}],"title":"Experimental Evaluation of the Scale Model Method to Simulate Lunar Vehicle Dynamics","stiType":"CONFERENCE_PAPER","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2017-01-31T14:44:04.7130000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20170000950,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Johnson, Kyle"},"organization":{"name":"NASA Glenn Research Center","location":"Cleveland, OH United States"}},"id":"60150ff5c1cf49b7a6fdebbf4cc90634"},{"sequence":1,"submissionId":20170000950,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Asnani, Vivake "},"organization":{"name":"NASA Glenn Research Center","location":"Cleveland, OH United States"}},"id":"aa4ea30e967c44bdb2b84de2f2593a52"},{"sequence":2,"submissionId":20170000950,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Polack, Jeff"},"organization":{"name":"NASA Glenn Research Center","location":"Cleveland, OH United States"}},"id":"1c9dac883e3d45cd880f2676cac5a6ad"},{"sequence":3,"submissionId":20170000950,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Plant, Mark"},"organization":{"name":"Youngstown State Univ.","location":"OH, United States"}},"id":"3a54f07b7bb64bc487a5b49aa40fee6f"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Conference Paper","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20170000950,"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":""},"created":"2017-01-31T14:44:04.7130000+00:00","center":{"code":"GRC","name":"Glenn Research Center","id":"19eeb25fa404421d9eaa5f876e853e3c"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"As compared to driving on Earth, the presence of lower gravity and uneven terrain on planetary bodies makes high speed driving difficult. In order to maintain ground contact and control vehicles need to be designed with special attention to dynamic response. The challenge of maintaining control on the Moon was evident during high speed operations of the Lunar Roving Vehicle (LRV) on Apollo 16, as at one point all four tires were off the ground; this event has been referred to as the Lunar Grand Prix. Ultimately, computer simulation should be used to examine these phenomena during the vehicle design process; however, experimental techniques are required for the validation and elucidation of key issues. The objectives of this study were to evaluate the methodology for developing a scale model of a lunar vehicle using similitude relationships and to test how vehicle configuration, six or eight wheel pods, and local tire compliance, soft or stiff, affect the vehicles dynamic performance. A wheel pod consists of a drive and steering transmission and wheel. The Lunar Electric Rover (LER), a human driven vehicle with a pressurized cabin, was selected as an example for which a scale model was built. The scaled vehicle was driven over an obstacle and the dynamic response was observed and then scaled to represent the full-size vehicle in lunar gravity. Loss of ground contact, in terms of vehicle travel distance with tires off the ground, was examined. As expected, local tire compliance allowed ground contact to be maintained over a greater distance. However, switching from a six-tire configuration to an eight-tire configuration with reduced suspension stiffness had a negative effect on ground contact. It is hypothesized that this was due to the increased number or frequency of impacts. The development and testing of this scale model provided practical lessons for future low-gravity vehicle development. ","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","meetings":[{"country":"United States","submissionId":20170000950,"endDate":"2016-09-14T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","sponsors":[{"organizationId":"be6ac801a9614c169809362091702ee5","meta":{"organization":{"name":"International Society for Terrain-Vehicle Systems","location":"Hanover, NH, United States"}},"meetingId":"b3be8d6ab9854245beffa8bf42bc5187","id":"eb970eb1bf4747a6a8ea376d066c390c"}],"name":"International Society for Terrain-Vehicle Systems (ISTV) Americas Regional Conference","location":"Detroit, MI","id":"b3be8d6ab9854245beffa8bf42bc5187","startDate":"2016-09-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20170000950,"id":"02408c4e2ef847ea8a731382cefa7e25","publicationDate":"2016-09-12T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"20170000950.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20170000950/downloads/20170000950.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20170000950/downloads/20170000950.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20170000950/downloads/20170000950.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-10-01-04-12"},{"_meta":{"score":186.98465},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"GOV_PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":19750021903,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"966b21945dfe42c9a3b9f2de3109c5f0","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Lunar And Planetary Exploration"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":19750021903,"ear":"NO","id":"374ce5aa088748009c4a63da11ddf79d","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2019-06-19T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","otherReportNumbers":["NASA-CR-143290","AD-A006518","AEWES-TR-M-71-7","Report Number: NASA-CR-143290","Report Number: AD-A006518","Report Number: AEWES-TR-M-71-7"],"title":"Effect of yaw angle on steering forces for the lunar roving vehicle wheel","stiType":"CONTRACTOR_REPORT","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2013-09-03T11:10:00.0000000+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":19750021903,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Green, A. J."},"organization":{"name":"Army Engineer Waterways Experiment Station","location":"Vicksburg, MS, United States"}},"id":"74c617f908434240ba92e2310fdd7bfa"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Contractor Report (CR)","technicalReviewType":"TECHNICAL_REVIEW_TYPE_NONE","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":19750021903,"legacyMeta":{"__type":"LegacyMetaIndex, StrivesApi.ServiceModel","accessionNumber":"75N29976"},"created":"2013-09-03T11:10:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"CDMS","name":"Legacy CDMS","id":"092d6e0881874968859b972d39a888dc"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"A series of tests was conducted with a Lunar Roving Vehicle (LRV) wheel operating at yaw angles ranging from -5 to +90 deg.  The load was varied from 42 to 82 lb (187 to 365 N), and the speed was varied from 3.5 to 10.0 ft/sec (1.07 to 3.05 m/sec).  It was noted that speed had an effect on side thrust and rut depth.  Side thrust, rut depth, and skid generally increased as the yaw angle increased.  For the range of loads used, the effect of load on performance was not significant.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","publications":[{"submissionId":19750021903,"id":"c17771984feb49eb8a61e4dbc4ea9c5f","publicationDate":"1974-10-01T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"19750021903.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/19750021903/downloads/19750021903.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/19750021903/downloads/19750021903.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/19750021903/downloads/19750021903.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-10-01-04-12"},{"_meta":{"score":162.77551},"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"containsIndication":false,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"PUBLIC_USE_PERMITTED","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"licenseType":"NO","submissionId":20220011974,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":false,"id":"48915c05b0c642ac916ee0dff3956e33","belongsToAuthors":false},"subjectCategories":["Lunar And Planetary Science And Exploration","Spacecraft Design, Testing And Performance"],"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"NO","submissionId":20220011974,"ear":"NO","id":"01c64ebadba94e088eefe2645f82a1b6","itar":"NO"},"distributionDate":"2022-08-12T05:00:00.0000000+00:00","fundingNumbers":[{"number":"10449.2.03.08.17.0958","submissionId":20220011974,"id":"092dbb140c6d489ea6f2f914c9448810","type":"TASK"}],"title":"Lunar Transport Vehicle Occupant Protection Requirements","stiType":"TECHNICAL_MEMORANDUM","distribution":"PUBLIC","submittedDate":"2022-08-04T17:06:22.6760200+00:00","authorAffiliations":[{"organizationId":"30956d12b05c56f99ba04cefabd82400","sequence":0,"submissionId":20220011974,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Kevin R. Dolick"},"organization":{"name":"KBR (United States)","location":"Houston, Texas, United States"}},"id":"98fea4e1620840deb642343e6f7b8a82","userType":"OTHER","userId":"1ed362676324426285d9de1f86a0239c"},{"organizationId":"00a2a0542f9451ffac4b0aa2053787b3","sequence":1,"submissionId":20220011974,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Jeffrey T. Somers"},"organization":{"name":"Johnson Space Center","location":"Houston, Texas, United States"}},"id":"9e3c2cea191747049b4edefdb0bec4d4","userType":"CIVIL","userId":"d9e217e94110429ab4bb9cc9dea91060"},{"organizationId":"30956d12b05c56f99ba04cefabd82400","sequence":2,"submissionId":20220011974,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Nathaniel J. Newby"},"organization":{"name":"KBR (United States)","location":"Houston, Texas, United States"}},"id":"1725371f7cfb444ba5f548a7ef7e8c35","userType":"CONTRACTOR_GRANTEE","userId":"4eeb3ac32d74400e91764ca8248292e5"},{"organizationId":"30956d12b05c56f99ba04cefabd82400","sequence":3,"submissionId":20220011974,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Teresa M. Reiber"},"organization":{"name":"KBR (United States)","location":"Houston, Texas, United States"}},"id":"e8f4414ef6974b4190ceb8a4eeeb714b","userType":"CONTRACTOR_GRANTEE","userId":"d8beb7d91c004206a7d80ec3103c02ab"},{"organizationId":"7f9c4cf9cb6f517db6b0fb40eb584c03","sequence":4,"submissionId":20220011974,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Bernard D. Adelstein"},"organization":{"name":"Ames Research Center","location":"Mountain View, California, United States"}},"id":"3dddb65196d94f8e9765d4ded63b3663","userType":"CIVIL","userId":"2d74e5991e6f4d95a3abc6956cc65731"},{"organizationId":"7f9c4cf9cb6f517db6b0fb40eb584c03","sequence":5,"submissionId":20220011974,"meta":{"author":{"orcidId":"","name":"Leeland Stone"},"organization":{"name":"Ames Research Center","location":"Mountain View, California, United States"}},"id":"25def2e499e04bcaa6a94067a7650496","userType":"CIVIL","userId":"19f406b3d4464b2580c78060ac2060c1"}],"stiTypeDetails":"Technical Memorandum (TM)","technicalReviewType":"NASA_TECHNICAL_MANAGEMENT","modified":"2025-08-31T18:39:21.7150190+00:00","id":20220011974,"created":"2022-08-04T16:39:15.5166950+00:00","center":{"code":"JSC","name":"Johnson Space Center","id":"dd46994b91a94cb2a2722617cbbadc55"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":2,"abstract":"The National Aeronautics and Space Administration (NASA) is preparing for future Artemis missions that will return humans to the lunar surface. A critical piece of these future missions is the Lunar Transport Vehicle (LTV), a transportation device to be used on the lunar surface. A vehicular method of transportation will allow for longer duration missions with increased capabilities to conduct research and transport soil, geological samples, or other materials of interest.\n\nMultiple missions to the lunar surface throughout the Apollo program also deployed the use of a lunar vehicle, known as the Lunar Roving Vehicle (LRV). The LRV was used during three of the six Apollo missions that successfully landed humans on the moon. Unfortunately, the LRV did not have any onboard instrumentation, and a large portion of the lunar performance evaluation relied on photographic documentation and crew reports. Therefore, we do not know the actual accelerations and vibrations experienced by the crew when driving on the lunar surface.\n\nThe objective of this document is to provide occupant protection guidance when designing the LTV. Acceleration, vibration, and jerk metrics imparted by the vehicle relative to the occupant shall not exceed those listed in this document. At the time of writing of these requirements, much of the LTV design is unknown. This document details requirements based on multiple possible restraint configurations and crew orientations.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","cui":{"isCui":false,"submissionId":20220011974,"id":"44e65a6e9b0a48f99a5b3b101542983d"},"publications":[{"submissionId":20220011974,"id":"847a81f7d8cf4f5f8c33713e19abad2a","publicationDate":"2022-09-01T04:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","name":"LTV manuscript v3.docx","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20220011974/downloads/LTV%20manuscript%20v3.docx","pdf":"/api/citations/20220011974/downloads/LTV%20manuscript%20v3.docx.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20220011974/downloads/LTV%20manuscript%20v3.docx.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-10-01-04-12"}],"aggregations":{"created":{"buckets":[{"key_as_string":"2013","key":1356998400000,"doc_count":22},{"key_as_string":"2023","key":1672531200000,"doc_count":5},{"key_as_string":"2022","key":1640995200000,"doc_count":4},{"key_as_string":"2024","key":1704067200000,"doc_count":4},{"key_as_string":"2025","key":1735689600000,"doc_count":2},{"key_as_string":"2017","key":1483228800000,"doc_count":1},{"key_as_string":"2018","key":1514764800000,"doc_count":1},{"key_as_string":"2026","key":1767225600000,"doc_count":1}]},"author":{"doc_count_error_upper_bound":1,"sum_other_doc_count":95,"buckets":[{"key":"Colin Creager","doc_count":3},{"key":"Heather Oravec","doc_count":3},{"key":"Abby Zinecker Howard","doc_count":2},{"key":"Costes, N. C.","